msgid "Wiki Editing Style Guide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:7
#: 97f274aaae294e06a1fb6c7f3132294f
msgid "This page explains some specific parts of syntax used by the wiki along with general style guidelines to promote consistency of appearance and maintainability of wiki content. The general rule is to keep things simple, using as little styling as possible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:9
#: 745cf82cf24f486aa6d9a71a498fd10b
msgid "For more information check out the `Sphinx reStructured Text Primer <http://www.sphinx-doc.org/en/stable/rest.html>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:13
#: d974cccb9f444d51bc825a2913a87805
msgid "Creating a new page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:17
#: 5d6c136edfef42a19fa4702c22620d17
msgid "First search the wiki to determine if there is already a wiki page about your topic — it is better to improve an existing topic than create a near-duplicate! Also discuss it with the `Wiki Editors on Discord <https://ardupilot.org/discord>`__ or enter an issue in the `Wiki issue list <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot_wiki/issues>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:23
#: 0e8bbbe31649475a9fb2a2059cab04c2
msgid "Pages should be created in the **/source/docs/** folder for your target wiki, given a \"descriptive\" name, and the file suffix \".rst\". Typically we use all lower case for filename, and separate words using \"-\" or \"_\". For example: **advanced-multicopter-design.rst**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:27
#: 59bc56d65ada4af3bf77e1f3d273fdea
msgid "Pages that are common to all wikis must be named with the prefix **common-** and must be created in **/common/source/docs/**. See :ref:`common_wiki_editing_guide_common_pages` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:30
#: 927f9c285b994deea3c4877e218d84c0
msgid "The title of the new page should be concise — informative enough that the reader can determine whether the topic is relevant and to differentiate it from other similar topics. The first letter of every word in the heading should be capitalized, with the exception of short connecting words like \"a\", \"with\", \"and\", \"the\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:35
#: f76685f827954647b359f647c60b48ac
msgid "The title should also be preceded by an anchor link named for the page. So the first information on the page would be:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:48
#: 8995aef3e4824dda82e787803193ade6
msgid "Working with common pages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:50
#: 20e66403023f4cb189e5eb05455eefb5
msgid "The wiki has a lot of information that is applicable to users of all the different vehicle types. In order to reduce (manual) duplication we define these topics in one place (**/common/source/docs**) and automatically copy them to other wikis where they are needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:55
#: 29a5d9c96b2e4369931957cad94a3190
msgid "Creating and editing common pages is similar to editing other pages except:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:57
#: 59ba6722a8b944a7b012949be7d38b9c
msgid "The filename of common pages must start with the text *common-*. For example, this page is **common-wiki_editing_guide.rst**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:59
#: 46d37a4428a148c0a4249cd9754ee016
msgid "All common pages must be stored in **/common/source/docs**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:60
#: 65affda4371241408c3b1794ffca03cc
msgid "The copywiki shortcode can be put at the end of the source to specify the set of destination wikis (use \"copywiki\" rather than \"xcopywiki\" below):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:67
#: cdec22c4a9d9424493144d6f18e9bd5a
msgid "If no copywiki shortcode is specified, common pages are automatically copied to the copter, plane, rover, and sub wikis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:70
#: 1870bc683dc949e4973b369ec962adaf
msgid "Vehicle-specific content can be added to the common topic using the ``site`` shortcode. Text that is not applicable to a target wiki is stripped out before the common page is copied to each wiki. The example below shows text that will only appear on rover and plane wikis (use site rather than xsite shown below!)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:79
#: 0d468cc90b38432388f0fa925974ff63
msgid "Always :ref:`link to other common topics <common-editor-information-resource_how_to_link_to_other_topics>` using relative linking. This ensures that you will link to the correct common topic when the wiki article is copied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:82
#: 75bc50af8f5448a0a7b8754a6045fc9b
msgid "Titles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:84
#: 099b802f9c8c43338e0b0c0d74ef0879
msgid "Choose a concise and specific title. It should be informative enough that a reader can determine if the content is likely to be relevant and yet differentiate it from other (similar) topics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:87
#: 3286dfe4840644cb9b9e5fc5fa19e350
msgid "Use first-letter capitalization for all words in the title (except connecting words: \"and\",\"the\", \"with\" etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-wiki-editing-style-guide.rst:89
#: 95e4d2ebf7f547b487cb04eb0889b979
msgid "The title syntax is as shown below. Note that we use an \"anchor reference\" immediately before the title (and named using the page filename). This allows us to link to the file from other wikis and from documents even if they move within the file structure."
msgstr ""

